  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the four files needed for this investigation:\n\n1. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/__init__.py`** \u2014 primary file: contains `install_src()`, which builds `collection_tar._ansible_normalized_cache` by stripping trailing `os.path.sep` from every member name (`m.name.removesuffix(os.path.sep): m for m in collection_tar.getmembers()`), and `_extract_tar_dir(tar, dirname, b_dest)`, which looks up `tar._ansible_normalized_cache[dirname]` after normalizing `dirname` the same way \u2014 the custom-cache mechanism the bug report describes.\n2. **`test/units/cli/galaxy/test_collection_extract_tar.py`** \u2014 existing unit test exercising `_extract_tar_dir` with a mocked tar object (not a real tarfile), showing the current test coverage gap: it never exercises a real `tarfile.TarFile` with actual member-name/lookup mismatches.\n3. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/collection/concrete_artifact_manager.py`** \u2014 defines `_tarfile_extract()`, the standard extraction contextmanager used elsewhere via `tar.extractfile(member)`/`tar.getmember()`, useful as the contrast case showing the standard-API path that doesn't need the custom cache.\n4. **`lib/ansible/galaxy/role.py`** \u2014 contains the sibling comment referencing the original CPython tarfile bug (`https://github.com/python/cpython/issues/107845`) that motivated this workaround, confirming point 3 of the report (the workaround predates a CPython fix).",
